# Hamro3D Mock Data Conventions

Apply these rules to every file in `app/data/`. This directory holds all Phase 0 mock data that will be replaced with API calls in Phase 1.

## Phase 0 Header Comment

Every mock file must begin with this JSDoc comment:

```typescript
/** Phase 0 mock — replace with API call in Phase 1 */
```

## File Naming

```
app/data/mock-{entity}.ts
```

| File | Entity covered |
|---|---|
| `mock-products.ts` | Piece / product catalogue |
| `mock-cart.ts` | Cart line items |
| `mock-wishlist.ts` | Wishlist product IDs |
| `mock-user-orders.ts` | Orders visible to authenticated users |
| `mock-admin-orders.ts` | Orders visible to admin |

New files follow the same pattern: `mock-{plural-entity}.ts`.

## Interface Naming

All interfaces in mock files use the `Mock` prefix:

```typescript
// Main entity interface
export interface MockUserOrder { ... }
export interface MockAdminOrder { ... }
export interface MockProduct { ... }

// Sub-interfaces for nested data
export interface MockUserOrderLineItem { ... }
export interface MockAdminOrderPayment { ... }
export interface MockUserOrderTimelineStep { ... }
```

## Status Types as Union Strings

Never use `enum`. Always use union string types:

```typescript
// Correct
export type MockUserOrderStatus = 'Processing' | 'In Progress' | 'Delivered' | 'Cancelled'
export type MockAdminOrderStatus = 'Pending' | 'Processing' | 'Shipped' | 'Delivered' | 'Cancelled'

// Wrong — never
enum OrderStatus { Processing, InProgress, Delivered, Cancelled }
```

## Required Exports per File

Every mock file must export these named exports, in this order:

```typescript
/** Phase 0 mock — replace with API call in Phase 1 */

// 1. Status union type (if applicable)
export type MockUserOrderStatus = 'Processing' | 'In Progress' | 'Delivered' | 'Cancelled'

// 2. Sub-interfaces (define before the main interface that uses them)
export interface MockUserOrderLineItem {
  productId: number
  name: string
  meta: string        // e.g. "Keychain · Matte Black · 1 piece"
  quantity: number
  price: number       // Raw NPR — never pre-formatted string
  image: string       // Path relative to /public
}

export interface MockUserOrderPayment {
  method: 'eSewa' | 'Khalti' | 'Cash on Delivery' | 'Bank Transfer'
  subtotal: number    // Raw NPR
  shipping: number    // Raw NPR
  total: number       // Raw NPR
}

export interface MockUserOrderTimelineStep {
  label: string
  date: string        // ISO 8601 or human-readable date string
  state: 'done' | 'active' | 'pending'
}

// 3. Main interface
export interface MockUserOrder {
  id: string                           // e.g. 'H3D-0001' — unique, no duplicates
  date: string                         // ISO 8601 string
  status: MockUserOrderStatus
  lines: MockUserOrderLineItem[]
  delivery: {
    address: string
    estimated: string                  // Human-readable: 'June 10–12, 2026'
  }
  payment: MockUserOrderPayment
  timeline: MockUserOrderTimelineStep[]
}

// 4. Data array — named mock{Entity}s (plural)
export const mockUserOrders: MockUserOrder[] = [
  {
    id: 'H3D-0001',
    // ...
  },
]

// 5. Lookup helper — getMock{Entity}ById
export function getMockUserOrderById(id: string): MockUserOrder | undefined {
  return mockUserOrders.find(o => o.id === id)
}

// 6. Utility functions (define once per file that needs them)
export function formatNprPrice(price: number): string {
  return `NPR ${price.toLocaleString('en-NP')}`
}
```

## No Duplicate IDs

Every mock entity must have a **globally unique `id`** within its array. IDs must not conflict across related files:

```typescript
// Wrong — duplicate IDs within same array
export const mockProducts = [
  { id: 7, name: 'Keychain' },
  { id: 8, name: 'Litholamp' },
  { id: 8, name: 'Nameplate' },  // DUPLICATE — forbidden
]

// Correct — all IDs unique
export const mockProducts = [
  { id: 7, name: 'Keychain' },
  { id: 8, name: 'Litholamp' },
  { id: 9, name: 'Nameplate' },
]
```

For order IDs, use the `H3D-` prefix with zero-padded sequential numbering:
- User orders: `H3D-0001`, `H3D-0002`, `H3D-0003`
- Product IDs: sequential integers starting at 1

## Price Storage Rule

**All prices are stored as raw integers (NPR). Never store a pre-formatted string.**

```typescript
// Correct — raw number
price: 1500   // NPR 1,500

// Wrong — pre-formatted string
price: 'NPR 1,500'
price: '1500.00'
```

Format at display time only:

```typescript
// In component or page
formatNprPrice(order.payment.total)  // → "NPR 4,500"
```

`formatNprPrice` is defined in the data file and imported where needed. Do not duplicate it across files — import from `mock-user-orders.ts` or `mock-admin-orders.ts` as the canonical source.

## Cross-File Reference Rules

If a mock order references a product, the `productId` must exist in `mock-products.ts`:

```typescript
// In mock-user-orders.ts
lines: [
  {
    productId: 3,  // Must exist as { id: 3, ... } in mock-products.ts
    name: 'Custom Photo Keychain',
    ...
  }
]
```

## TypeScript Strictness

Mock data arrays must be typed with their interface — never `any` or implicit `object[]`:

```typescript
// Correct
export const mockUserOrders: MockUserOrder[] = [ ... ]

// Or readonly if the data should never be mutated
export const mockProducts: ReadonlyArray<MockProduct> = [ ... ]

// Wrong
export const mockUserOrders = [ ... ]         // implicit any[]
export const mockUserOrders: any[] = [ ... ]  // explicit any — forbidden
```
